Subject: [PATCH 1/2] 6th grade: the Clock Tower (unit 4, exponents and order
 of operations)

Chimes (meaning of exponents, powers of whole numbers, powers of
fractions and decimals), Gears (order of operations without and with
exponents), and Clock Face (order of operations with fractions and
exponents, comparing powers). A small exact order-of-operations engine
builds every problem: a "what do you do first?" choice when there is a
real wrong first step, then one step per operation with the part being
worked on highlighted. 7 Khan skills and 8 new mix-ups, including
working left to right and ignoring parentheses. Opens after the Market
Stall Unit Test.

